+
+A relevant favorable comparison can support reusing a decision within its observed scope. Check whether that decision is already represented in the current Parent; a past Retain is not proof of current presence and does not justify another copy. A relevant adverse or mixed comparison should inform which part to retain, narrow, redirect or withdraw. Do not preserve an entire proposal merely by adding an uncertainty disclaimer, and do not treat evidence against one strategy as proof that a replacement works.
